# Placeholder template. Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in the real values —
# never commit `.env` itself. See CLAUDE.md / .githooks/pre-commit.

# ── The dev database, named here only so the drop-guard can see it ────────────
#
# This package runs no service, so nothing here dials MONGODB_URI: the integration project is handed
# its own URL, assembled from the MONGO_TEST_* block below, under this very name.
#
# It is in the template because `buildTestMongoUrl` in vitest.mongo.mts compares MONGO_TEST_DB
# against the database MONGODB_URI points at and refuses to run when they are the same — globalSetup
# drops that database, and the dev and test databases live on one cluster with only the name telling
# them apart. That comparison reads the value dotenv loaded from `.env`, before the integration
# project overrides the variable. Leave it empty and the guard is inert: `dbNameFromUri('')` is
# empty, the check short-circuits, and the one typo it exists to catch goes through.
#
# So: same value as the nine services' MONGODB_URI — the dev URI, dbMarketplaceDev. It is a
# credential; it belongs in the gitignored `.env` and never here.
MONGODB_URI=

# ── Integration tests: real MongoDB (MONGO_TEST_*) ────────────────────────────
#
# `yarn test:int` needs this whole block or it fails fast with a clear
# "Missing MONGO_TEST_*" message (see vitest.mongo.mts / test/integration/globalSetup.mts)
# instead of a stack trace or a connection timeout.
#
# Copy the four user/password values from marketplace-db-setup/.env — it is the same cluster and
# the same two users. The database name is this package’s own.
#
# Two users on purpose, the same split production uses:
#   OWNER — dbOwner. test/integration/globalSetup.mts drops MONGO_TEST_DB before the
#           suite runs. This package has no migrations of its own to replay (that is
#           marketplace-db-setup's job, and it is only exercised by the services' own
#           integration suites) — dropping the database is the entire setup step here.
#   R/W   — readWrite. test/integration/models.int.test.mts connects with this one, so
#           a schema that quietly needs more than readWrite fails in the suite instead
#           of in production.
#
# ⚠️ THREE variables name the test database and all three must carry the SAME name:
# MONGO_TEST_DB, MONGO_TEST_AUTH_ADMIN, and the database path of MONGO_TEST_CONN_STRING.
# vitest.mongo.mts refuses to build a URL when they disagree, because it rebuilds the path from
# MONGO_TEST_DB — a connection string naming a different database would still connect, and the
# suite would drop a database that string never mentioned.
#
# The name below belongs to this package alone; no other repo may reuse it, since every
# suite drops its own database.
#
# authSource is therefore the test database itself, NOT `admin`: both users have to be created in
# it, with a role on it — see marketplace-db-setup/setup/mongodb.js. Dropping the database does not
# delete them; MongoDB keeps every user in admin.system.users whatever its auth database is.
#
# Shape: mongodb+srv://<host>/dbMarketplaceTestCommon   (credentials are injected from the pairs below)
MONGO_TEST_CONN_STRING=
MONGO_TEST_AUTH_ADMIN=dbMarketplaceTestCommon

# DB OWNER USER
MONGO_TEST_UDBOWNER=
MONGO_TEST_PWDDBOWNER=

# R/W USER
MONGO_TEST_UDBRW=
MONGO_TEST_PWDDBRW=

MONGO_TEST_DB=dbMarketplaceTestCommon


